" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.852</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">R Square</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.734</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.725</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Adjusted R Square</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.678</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.668</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td colspan="5" rowspan="1"><hr/></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">F statistics</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">13.238a</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">12.670a</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn3-ijerph-06-01075"><p><list list-type="bullet"><list-item><p>Independent variables of (ln) denote the natural logarithm.</p></list-item><list-item><p>Dependent variables, RES&#x00026;BRO and RESPIRATORY, are the natural logarithm.</p></list-item><list-item><p>Significance of t-statistics is indicated by the following: &#x0201c;a&#x0201d; at the 1% level, &#x0201c;b&#x0201d; at the 5% level, and &#x0201c;c&#x0201d; at the 10% level.</p></list-item><list-item><p>TIME dummy 1998 is an omitted variable to evaluate the implementation of the new tire recycling regulation since 1999.</p></list-item><list-item><p>Another regression included the variable of population density that was not statistically significant and showed similar results with lower F statistics. The results are available from the author on request.</p></list-item></list></p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>